IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 (housing costs element for renters): paragraphs 1 and 2 (introduction and
-- interpretation) and Part 2 (the exception for 16 and 17 year old care leavers).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- The definitions in paragraph 2 that only point somewhere else are not rules here: "extended benefit unit", "non-dependant" (paragraph 9),
-- "housing cost contribution" (paragraph 13), "relevant payments" (paragraph 3), "renter who requires overnight care" (paragraph 12),
-- "shared accommodation" (paragraph 27) and "joint renter" and "renter" (paragraph 1(2), below) are encoded where the text defines them;
-- "domestic violence" is regulation 98(4) (uc4); "exempt accommodation", "relative", "social housing", "member of the armed forces",
-- "Housing Act functions" and "the Rent Officers Order 2013" rest on instruments that are not among the inputs and are stated inputs
-- where a rule needs them. The rows of the coverage table in NOTES.md say which.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 1(1) and (2): who is a renter. Whether regulation 26(2) applies to a claimant is regulation 26 (uc1), taken as a fact.
-- src:2131 | (1) This Schedule contains provisions about claimants to whom regulation 26(2) applies.
-- src:2132 | (2) Claimants who fall within sub-paragraph (1) are referred to in this Schedule as “renters” (and references to “joint renters” are to joint claimants to whom regulation 26(2) applies).
@ref Sch 4 para 1(1) and (2) (src:2131-2132)
DECLARE `Claimant who may be a renter` HAS
    -- out of range: reg 26(2) (piece uc1)
    `regulation 26(2) applies to the claimant`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim basis`                                 IS A `Claim basis`

-- src:2131 | (1) This Schedule contains provisions about claimants to whom regulation 26(2) applies.
-- src:2132 | (2) Claimants who fall within sub-paragraph (1) are referred to in this Schedule as “renters” (and references to “joint renters” are to joint claimants to whom regulation 26(2) applies).
@ref Sch 4 para 1(1) and (2) (src:2131-2132)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant who may be a renter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 1(2) — a claimant is a renter` claimant MEANS
    claimant's `regulation 26(2) applies to the claimant`

-- src:2132 | (2) Claimants who fall within sub-paragraph (1) are referred to in this Schedule as “renters” (and references to “joint renters” are to joint claimants to whom regulation 26(2) applies).
@ref Sch 4 para 1(2) "joint renters" (src:2132)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant who may be a renter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 1(2) — a joint renter` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `regulation 26(2) applies to the claimant`)
    AND (claimant's `claim basis` EQUALS `joint claimants`)

-- Paragraph 1(4): the calculation is made under Part 4 for a renter in the private rented sector and under Part 5 for a renter in the social
-- rented sector. Paragraphs 17, 20 and 30 decide which; this type is their answer.
-- src:2134 | (4) The following Parts of this Schedule provide for the calculation of the amount of housing costs element to be included under regulation 26(2) in a renter's award of universal credit—
-- src:2135 | (a) Part 3 contains general provisions that apply to all calculations, whether under Part 4 or Part 5;
-- src:2136 | (b) Part 4 applies in relation to renters who occupy accommodation in the private rented sector...; and
-- src:2137 | (c) Part 5 applies in relation to renters who occupy accommodation in the social rented sector....
@ref Sch 4 para 1(4) (src:2134-2137)
DECLARE `Part of Schedule 4 under which the housing costs element is calculated` IS ONE OF
    `Part 4 (private rented sector)`
    `Part 5 (social rented sector)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 2, "listed persons" in relation to a renter: the renter; where the renter is a member of a couple, the other member; and any
-- child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible.
-- src:2146 | “listed persons”, in relation to a renter, means—
-- src:2147 | (a) the renter;
-- src:2148 | (b) where the renter is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple; and
-- src:2149 | (c) any child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible;
@ref Sch 4 para 2 "listed persons" (src:2146-2149)
DECLARE `Person who may be a listed person` HAS
    `the renter`                                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple of which the renter is a member`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 4 (piece uc1), "responsible for a child or qualifying young person"
    `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2146 | “listed persons”, in relation to a renter, means—
-- src:2147 | (a) the renter;
-- src:2148 | (b) where the renter is a member of a couple, the other member of the couple; and
-- src:2149 | (c) any child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible;
@ref Sch 4 para 2 "listed persons" (src:2146-2149)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be a listed person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 2 — a listed person` person MEANS
    (person's `the renter`)
    OR (person's `the other member of the couple of which the renter is a member`)
    OR (person's `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter (or either joint renter) is responsible`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 2, "registered social landlord": registered in either of two registers (Wales; Scotland).
-- src:2157 | “registered social landlord” means—
-- src:2158 | (a) a body which is registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996 ;
-- src:2159 | (b) a body which is registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010 ;
@ref Sch 4 para 2 "registered social landlord" (src:2157-2159)
DECLARE `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord` HAS
    `registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2157 | “registered social landlord” means—
-- src:2158 | (a) a body which is registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996 ;
-- src:2159 | (b) a body which is registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010 ;
@ref Sch 4 para 2 "registered social landlord" (src:2157-2159)
GIVEN landlord IS A `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 2 — registered social landlord` landlord MEANS
    (landlord's `registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996`)
    OR (landlord's `registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010`)

-- Paragraph 2, "provider of social housing": a local authority (regulation 2's definition, the keel's rule), a non-profit registered provider,
-- in relation to accommodation which is social housing a profit-making registered provider, or a registered social landlord.
-- Whether a provider is registered, and whether accommodation is "social housing" (sections 68 to 77 of the Housing and Regeneration Act
-- 2008), are stated inputs.
-- src:2152 | “provider of social housing” means—
-- src:2153 | (a) a local authority;
-- src:2154 | (b) a non-profit registered provider of social housing;
-- src:2155 | (c) in relation to accommodation which is social housing, a profit-making registered provider of social housing;
-- src:2156 | (d) a registered social landlord;
@ref Sch 4 para 2 "provider of social housing" (src:2152-2156)
DECLARE `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing` HAS
    `the landlord as a possible local authority`                           IS A `Body that may be a local authority`
    `non-profit registered provider of social housing`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `profit-making registered provider of social housing`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accommodation is social housing`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord`                IS A `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord`

-- src:2152 | “provider of social housing” means—
-- src:2153 | (a) a local authority;
-- src:2154 | (b) a non-profit registered provider of social housing;
-- src:2155 | (c) in relation to accommodation which is social housing, a profit-making registered provider of social housing;
-- src:2156 | (d) a registered social landlord;
@ref Sch 4 para 2 "provider of social housing" (src:2152-2156)
GIVEN landlord IS A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` landlord MEANS
    (`reg 2 — local authority` (landlord's `the landlord as a possible local authority`))
    OR (landlord's `non-profit registered provider of social housing`)
    OR ((landlord's `profit-making registered provider of social housing`) AND (landlord's `the accommodation is social housing`))
    OR (`Sch 4 para 2 — registered social landlord` (landlord's `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2, paragraph 4: section 11(1) of the Act (housing costs) does not apply to a renter who is 16 or 17 years old and is a care leaver.
-- The answer TRUE means that the renter gets no housing costs element calculated under this Schedule. "Care leaver" is regulation 8 (uc1).
-- For joint renters the text says "any renter"; the rule is asked of one renter at a time (fork U3-F7).
-- src:2177 | Section 11(1) of the Act (housing costs) does not apply to any renter who is 16 or 17 years old and is a care leaver.
@ref Sch 4 para 4 (src:2177)
DECLARE `Renter who may be a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` HAS
    `age in complete years`                                  IS A NUMBER
    -- out of range: reg 8 (piece uc1), "care leaver"
    `care leaver`                                            IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2177 | Section 11(1) of the Act (housing costs) does not apply to any renter who is 16 or 17 years old and is a care leaver.
@ref Sch 4 para 4 (src:2177)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter who may be a 16 or 17 year old care leaver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 4 — the renter gets no housing costs element as a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` renter MEANS
    (renter's `age in complete years` AT LEAST 16)
    AND (renter's `age in complete years` AT MOST 17)
    AND (renter's `care leaver`)
